    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (78.68) and **Junior Caminero** (76.88) serving as our primary anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start against a mediocre Flaherty, with his elite 0.444 xwOBA driving a high-floor performance, while **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.85 for Kelly, paired with a prime #3 hole assignment that inflates his scoring. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first philosophy; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.03) is a tactical play today, as his favorable platoon advantage against Woodruff and the potential for a stolen base against a slow-delivering pitcher make him a superior start despite the sub-par SP matchup.\n\nOur decision to bench **Jacob Gonzalez** (42.11) was the most difficult call of the morning; while he cleared the floor, he failed to crack our top-12 due to a suboptimal #9 batting position and adverse wind conditions affecting the ballpark. Elsewhere, we are monitoring **Caleb Durbin** (58.79) closely, as his status remains pending. Should his lineup spot fall lower than the assumed #6, his efficiency score may dip, but his neutral platoon advantage against Rod\u00f3n keeps him in the mix. We are exercising caution with **Christian Yelich** (55.76); while his #1 spot is valuable, the sharp negative adjustment for his platoon matchup against Rolison limits his ceiling, necessitating a careful watch on his early-game at-bats. Our remaining bench\u2014including **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, and **Casey Schmitt**\u2014remains excluded from the active roster as they failed to meet our internal 40.0 efficiency floor, largely due to intimidating matchups against arms like Luzardo and Sale.",
